{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayoutValueKey","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you create a custom layout by defining a type that conforms to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol, you can also create custom layout values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that you set on individual views, and that your container view can access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to guide its layout behavior. Your custom values resemble","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the built-in layout values that you set with view modifiers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/layoutPriority(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/zIndex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but have a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"purpose that you define.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To create a custom layout value, define a type that conforms to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LayoutValueKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol and implement the one required property that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns the default value of the property. For example, you can create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a property that defines an amount of flexibility for a view, defined as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an optional floating point number with a default value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["private struct Flexibility: LayoutValueKey {","    static let defaultValue: CGFloat? = nil","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift compiler infers this particular key’s associated type as an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/CoreFoundation\/CGFloat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from this definition.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Set-a-value-on-a-view","level":3,"text":"Set a value on a view"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set the value on a view by adding the ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/layoutValue(key:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view modifier to the view. To make your custom value easier to work","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with, you can do this in a convenience modifier in an extension of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["extension View {","    func layoutFlexibility(_ value: CGFloat?) -> some View {","        layoutValue(key: Flexibility.self, value: value)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use your modifier to set the value on any views that need a nondefault","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack {","    Text(\"One View\")","    Text(\"Another View\")","        .layoutFlexibility(3)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any view that you don’t explicitly set a value for uses the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value, as with the first ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\